[150,439,317],{}," env var (",[150,442,443],{},"{ \"userId\": 42 }"," →\n",[150,446,447],{},"USER_ID=42",") plus ",[150,450,321],{}," with the full JSON. Static ",[150,453,288],{}," wins over data-derived vars.\nTwo data keys that map to the same env var (",[150,456,457],{},"fooBar"," and ",[150,460,461],{},"foo_bar",[150,463,464],{},"FOO_BAR",") are an error:\nconfig validation fails fast at load time, and a run that slips through fails instead of\nsilently last-write-wins.",[159,467,469],{"id":468},"exit-codes","Exit codes",[164,471,472,482],{},[167,473,474],{},[170,475,476,479],{},[173,477,478],{},"Exit",[173,480,481],{},"Result",[186,483,484,496,511],{},[170,485,486,491],{},[191,487,488],{},[150,489,490],{},"0",[191,492,493],{},[150,494,495],{},"succeeded",[170,497,498,501],{},[191,499,500],{},"non-zero",[191,502,503,506,507,510],{},[150,504,505],{},"failed"," with ",[150,508,509],{},"exit N"," + tail of the log",[170,512,513,516],{},[191,514,515],{},"timeout",[191,517,518,519],{},"SIGTERM → SIGKILL → ",[150,520,341],{},[146,522,523,526,527,529,530,533,534,537],{},[150,524,525],{},"config.timeoutMs: -1"," disables the container timeout entirely — the process\nruns until it exits on its own or is cancelled manually. (Before daemon 0.11.0 a\n",[150,528,345],{}," was passed straight into ",[150,531,532],{},"setTimeout"," and killed the container instantly\nwith ",[150,535,536],{},"timeout after -1ms",".)",[159,539,541,542,545],{"id":540},"stdio-contract-envelope-true-experimental","Stdio contract (",[150,543,544],{},"envelope: true",") — experimental",[547,548,549],"blockquote",{},[146,550,551,553,554,558],{},[205,552,408],{}," The ",[387,555,557],{"href":556},"process","process runner"," ships a reference worker for the\nstdio contract; a container image that speaks it is not published yet. Enable it\nwhen your own image implements the contract (see below) — exit-code mode remains\nthe default and is unchanged.",[146,560,561,562,566],{},"Opt-in protocol mode for containers that want to report progress and results\nstructurally. The container speaks the ",[387,563,565],{"href":564},"..\u002Fprotocol#stdio-transport","stdio transport",":",[418,568,569,587,600,609],{},[421,570,571,574,575,578,579,582,583,586],{},[205,572,573],{},"request"," — one JSON envelope ",[150,576,577],{},"{ \"task\": { \"name\", \"config\" }, \"data\" }"," on\n",[205,580,581],{},"stdin"," (",[150,584,585],{},"docker run -i",", attached automatically), then EOF",[421,588,589,592,593,596,597],{},[205,590,591],{},"progress"," — NDJSON lines on ",[205,594,595],{},"stdout",": intermediate\n",[150,598,599],{},"{ \"status\": \"running\", \"progress\": 42 }",[421,601,602,605,606,608],{},[205,603,604],{},"result"," — one terminal line on ",[205,607,595],{}," (same envelope shape as the process\nrunner \u002F HTTP runner)",[421,610,611,614,615,618],{},[205,612,613],{},"logs"," — anything else on ",[205,616,617],{},"stderr"," (never stdout — stdout is the protocol)",[620,621,626],"pre",{"className":622,"code":623,"language":624,"meta":625,"style":625},"language-json shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter vitesse-light vitesse-dark","{ \"runner\": \"docker\", \"config\": { \"image\": \"registry\u002Fmy-worker\", \"envelope\": true, \"data\": { \"videoId\": \"v-42\" } } }\n","json","",[150,627,628],{"__ignoreMap":625},[248,629,632,636,640,644,647,649,652,655,657,660,662,664,666,668,671,673,676,678,680,682,685,687,689,691,693,695,697,701,703,705,707,709,711,713,715,719,721,723,725,728,730,733,735],{"class":630,"line":631},"line",1,[248,633,635],{"class":634},"soVBu","{",[248,637,639],{"class":638},"s4Jsk"," \"",[248,641,643],{"class":642},"sLorS","runner",[248,645,646],{"class":638},"\"",[248,648,566],{"class":634},[248,650,639],{"class":651},"sbYkP",[248,653,152],{"class":654},"sTbE_",[248,656,646],{"class":651},[248,658,659],{"class":634},",",[248,661,639],{"class":638},[248,663,161],{"class":642},[248,665,646],{"class":638},[248,667,566],{"class":634},[248,669,670],{"class":634}," {",[248,672,639],{"class":638},[248,674,195],{"class":675},"sa2tF",[248,677,646],{"class":638},[248,679,566],{"class":634},[248,681,639],{"class":651},[248,683,684],{"class":654},"registry\u002Fmy-worker",[248,686,646],{"class":651},[248,688,659],{"class":634},[248,690,639],{"class":638},[248,692,397],{"class":675},[248,694,646],{"class":638},[248,696,566],{"class":634},[248,698,700],{"class":699},"s8XtY"," true",[248,702,659],{"class":634},[248,704,639],{"class":638},[248,706,299],{"class":675},[248,708,646],{"class":638},[248,710,566],{"class":634},[248,712,670],{"class":634},[248,714,639],{"class":638},[248,716,718],{"class":717},"skNjk","videoId",[248,720,646],{"class":638},[248,722,566],{"class":634},[248,724,639],{"class":651},[248,726,727],{"class":654},"v-42",[248,729,646],{"class":651},[248,731,732],{"class":634}," }",[248,734,732],{"class":634},[248,736,737],{"class":634}," }\n",[146,739,740,741,743],{},"A container that opted in but exits without a terminal envelope is a broken worker: the\nrun fails with a clear protocol error. A container without ",[150,742,397],{}," keeps the plain\nexit-code mapping — the two modes never mix.",[159,745,747],{"id":746},"private-registries-auth","Private registries (auth)",[146,749,750,751,582,754,756,757,760,761,566],{},"The runner spawns the ",[205,752,753],{},"docker CLI",[150,755,156],{},"), not the docker HTTP API — so\nCLI credential resolution applies. ",[150,758,759],{},"docker run"," pulls an image that is not present\nlocally, and that implicit pull authenticates exactly like ",[150,762,763],{},"docker pull",[418,765,766,788,806,813],{},[421,767,768,771,772,775,776,779,780,783,784,787],{},[205,769,770],{},"The CLI must exist in the daemon's image."," The official ",[150,773,774],{},"sched-daemon"," image\nships ",[150,777,778],{},"docker-cli"," (added 2026-08-22 after books' T2 finding); a custom\u002Fcomposed\nimage that drops it needs ",[150,781,782],{},"apk add docker-cli"," (alpine) — otherwise every\ndocker task fails with ",[150,785,786],{},"ENOENT"," at spawn.",[421,789,790,793,794,797,798,801,802,805],{},[150,791,792],{},"$DOCKER_CONFIG\u002Fconfig.json"," (default ",[150,795,796],{},"~\u002F.docker\u002Fconfig.json",") — mount it into the\ndaemon's container (",[150,799,800],{},"\u002Froot\u002F.docker\u002Fconfig.json",") or point ",[150,803,804],{},"DOCKER_CONFIG"," at a volume.",[421,807,808,809,812],{},"The same file that ",[150,810,811],{},"docker login"," writes — no sched-side config, no env creds.",[421,814,815,816,819],{},"Works unchanged behind a read-only docker-socket proxy (",[150,817,818],{},"DOCKER_HOST","): credentials\nare a CLI-side concern, the proxy passes the pull through.",[146,821,822,823,582,826,829,830,833,834,836,837,839],{},"The image allowlist is matched ",[205,824,825],{},"by name\u002Fcommand string only",[150,827,828],{},"image[@command]",");\nregistry auth never affects allowlist matching or tag resolution (default ",[150,831,832],{},":latest",",\nexplicit ",[150,835,219],{}," wins — pure string logic). The actual tag dereference happens at pull\ntime inside the docker daemon, which is exactly where the credentials apply. A pull\nthat fails auth surfaces as a run failure (",[150,838,759],{}," exits non-zero with the\nregistry's 401 in the log).",[159,841,843,844,212],{"id":842},"security-sandbox-allowedtools","Security: sandbox (",[150,845,372],{},[146,847,848,849,851,852,855,856,858,859,862,863,866],{},"The runner is constrained by the sandbox ceiling — pass ",[150,850,372],{}," when\ncreating the runner (or set it in the daemon build \u002F tasks.json ",[150,853,854],{},"runners"," block,\nsee ",[387,857,390],{"href":389},"). Exact names and trailing wildcards are supported:\n",[150,860,861],{},"allowedTools: ['alpine:*', 'ghcr.io\u002Fmy-org\u002F*']",". A task whose image\u002Fcommand is\nnot allowed fails fast ",[205,864,865],{},"before"," any container is spawned.",[146,868,869,870,873,874,876,877,880],{